# Human heart sounds
heart-stethoscope-human-healthy = You hear a steady lub-dub. The heart sounds healthy.
heart-stethoscope-human-damaged = You hear an irregular rhythm with a faint murmur.

# Arachnid heart sounds (copper-based hemocyanin)
heart-stethoscope-arachnid-healthy = You hear a soft, rhythmic hissing as hemolymph circulates.
heart-stethoscope-arachnid-damaged = You hear an irregular, sluggish hissing.

# Vox heart sounds (ammonia-based blood)
heart-stethoscope-vox-healthy = You hear a thin, reedy gurgle as ammonia blood pumps.
heart-stethoscope-vox-damaged = You hear a weak, sputtering gurgle.

# Diona heart sounds (plant sap vascular flow - diffuse, no distinct heart)
heart-stethoscope-diona-healthy = You hear a slow woody creaking and sap trickling.
heart-stethoscope-diona-damaged = You hear a strained creaking and diminished flow.

# Moth heart sounds (hemolymph)
heart-stethoscope-moth-healthy = You hear a faint, rapid fluttering.
heart-stethoscope-moth-damaged = You hear a weak, erratic flutter.

# Reptilian heart sounds (cold-blooded, slower)
heart-stethoscope-reptilian-healthy = You hear a very slow, deep thump.
heart-stethoscope-reptilian-damaged = You hear an irregular, shallow thump.

# Slime heart sounds (slime fluid)
heart-stethoscope-slime-healthy = You hear a wet squelching rhythm.
heart-stethoscope-slime-damaged = You hear a watery, irregular slosh.
